From d094b2b4abf77e49b1f6c460d3601634850ded3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Pukhov <alex.m.pukhov@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:30:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Rectilinear meshes: gridCoordinates and coordinate data
 sets

Support for meshes with explicit, non-equidistant coordinates along some
axes (openPMD-standard issue #142, proposal for 2.0):

- Iteration::gridCoordinates: container of 1D coordinate data sets in the
  group <basePath>gridCoordinates/ of an iteration; written only if not
  empty, read if present.
- Mesh::gridCoordinates() / setGridCoordinates(): per axis an empty string
  (regular axis) or the absolute path of a coordinate data set;
  MeshRecordComponent::setGridCoordinates() for staggered components.
- Iteration::gridCoordinatesPath(name) and gridCoordinatesOf(mesh[, comp])
  to build and resolve the references.
- Python bindings (Iteration.grid_coordinates, grid_coordinates_path,
  grid_coordinates_of, Mesh.grid_coordinates, Mesh_Record_Component
  .grid_coordinates), examples 3c_write_rectilinear_serial (C++, Python),
  C++ test rectilinear_meshes (group- and file-based, staggered component,
  regular mesh, dangling reference), Python round trip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DRiRr7s6YoyWRd6EM8Zzbz
